          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Cordelia\",\"addressee\":\"Lear\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Unhappy that I am, I cannot heave\\nMy heart into my mouth: I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you, Your Majesty.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly avows Cordelia’s love for Lear as a present emotional and relational state. The continuation qualifies its measure but does not remove its truth-presenting force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.88,\"reason\":\"The expression, as immediately qualified, invokes Cordelia’s existing filial bond and presents her love as fulfilling that obligation. It does not clearly create a new promise or future commitment, so undertaking force is moderate rather than dominant.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I\\nReturn those duties back as are right fit,\\nObey you, love you, and most honour you.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The target is a measured avowal framed by Cordelia’s deliberate limitation of what she will say, not a reflex-like or affectively discharged cry. Her difficulty verbalising her heart does not itself make the focal words an expressive outburst.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Unhappy that I am, I cannot heave\\nMy heart into my mouth: I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"The target’s core force is adequately represented by avowal of love together with invocation of an existing filial bond. The respectful form of address does not establish a separate residual mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"In a public division of the kingdom, Lear asks each daughter to say how much she loves him, linking the answer to his bounty. Cordelia answers Lear as both father and king. Her focal avowal is deliberately restrained and is immediately measured by her filial bond rather than expanded into the competitive declaration Lear solicits.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Cordelia invokes an already existing filial obligation: she loves, obeys, and honours Lear as duties she considers fitting. The focal expression does not clearly make a new promise. Lear does not accept the restrained formulation as satisfactory; he asks her to amend it and warns that it may damage her fortunes.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passage is recognised as the opening court scene of Shakespeare’s King Lear.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence supports the utterance’s avowal and bond-invoking force, but it does not by itself settle every aspect of Cordelia’s inner emotional state or any consequences beyond the supplied scene excerpt.\"}"
